287 4 "// first (queue 210: they were copied off the stack, then again behind self)"] [303 51 "// next(gen()): the generator dies at the return (queue 297)"] [326 3 "// CPython's RETURN_GENERATOR: the frame kept in its generator, coroutine or async generator"] [335 1 "// directMax bounds the direct calls (callDirect) nested on the thread's Go stack at once: each holds its caller's Go"] [336 1 "// frames while its callee runs, so a deeper chain (a recursion past it, up to any recursion limit) goes on as pushed"] [337 1 "// frames, in the innermost loop, with no Go frames per Python call (queue 216d)."] [340 1 "// enter is a call's callee frame (made, its arguments bound) run from f: when f and the callee are both compiled,"] [341 1 "// directly by f's own Go code (callDirect: its value pushed on f's stack, or its exception returned); else returned"] [342 1 "// as the thread's *pushFrame, read by runFrames before the thread's next call."] [351 1 "// callDirect runs callee, a compiled function's frame called by f's compiled code (queue 216d, the user's (a) on"] [352 1 "// 216's DECISION 1): a loop of its own (runFrames, direct) with callee its entry frame, entered as runFrames enters a"] [353 1 "// pushed frame (f_back f, the recursion limit's check raising in f, the eval breaker's error in callee, no C level),"] [354 1 "// so its exception unwinds through callee's handlers and leaves it with callee's traceback entry, then f's code"] [355 1 "// returns it and f's loop adds f's; its value pushed on f's stack, or callInit's instance (an __init__ returning"] [356 1 "// anything but None the TypeError raised in f), as runFrames pushes a returning pushed frame's."] [366 1 "// runDirect is callDirect's run of callee from the running frame's compiled code: its value (callInit's instance for"] [367 1 "// an __init__), or its exception, returned to that code."] [386 1 "// callInit is the call of a class whose __init__ runs in the caller's loop (initInline; queue 210, CPython 3.